{"id":"ENG-1847","title":"Define shared cross-app node content contract","description":"## Problem

* Roam and Obsidian do not yet have a precise shared payload contract for cross-app node discovery, import, and refresh.
* Destination apps need stable source identity plus compatible `direct` title and `full` markdown content variants.
* App-specific implementation work will be hard to split cleanly without a typed contract and fixtures.

## Solution

* Define the shared node contract for source app, source space, source-local ID, stable RID/origin identity, title, markdown body, and modified timestamp.
* Add Roam-origin and Obsidian-origin fixtures/examples that use `direct` and `full` content variants.
* Document known markdown fidelity limits and keep atJSON positioned as a future replacement, not an MVP0 blocker.

## Done When

* Shared types/helpers or contract docs describe the required cross-app node payload.
* Fixtures cover one Roam-origin node and one Obsidian-origin node with stable identity and markdown content.
* Follow-up Roam and Obsidian implementation tickets can reference this contract without redefining payload shape.

eg

```
// just an example, not strict

type SharedNodePayload = {
    sourceApp: "roam" | "obsidian";
    sourceSpaceId: string;
    sourceSpaceName: string;
    sourceLocalNodeId: string;
    sourceRid: string;

    nodeType: {
      sourceLocalId: string;
      label: string;
    };

    content: {
        value: string;
      };
      full: {
        format: "text/markdown";
        value: string;
      };
    };

    sourceModifiedAt: string;
  };

  const roamOriginClaim = {
    sourceApp: "roam",
    sourceSpaceName: "MAP Lab",
    sourceLocalNodeId: "tgWb6JozF",
    sourceRid: "roam:MAP Lab:tgWb6JozF", // just example, use RID format that is already being used
    nodeType: {
      sourceLocalId: "claim",
      label: "Claim",
    },
    content: {
      direct: {
      },
      full: {
        format: "text/markdown",
        value: "# CLM - Sleep improves memory consolidation\n\nEvidence suggests...",
      },
    },
    sourceModifiedAt: "2026-06-12T14:00:00.000Z",
  };
```

## Out of Scope

* Implementing Roam share UI or Obsidian/Roam import materialization.
* Implementing relation, asset, schema-collision, or refresh behavior.
* Adding atJSON conversion.

## Notes

* Functional requirements: [F2: Bidirectional node content persistence](<https://roamresearch.com/#/app/discourse-graphs/page/8kcJHU3Hl>), [F3: Markdown-first content model](<https://roamresearch.com/#/app/discourse-graphs/page/CJq0kR3t4>), [F9: Stable cross-app identity](<https://roamresearch.com/#/app/discourse-graphs/page/914EWeU_9>).
* Related follow-ups: Roam emits `full` markdown, Roam single-node share action, Obsidian source contract validation.
